why Every Alliance quest of Krol'dok Stronghold in one run, with the Riverglades chain that opens them.

# Krol'dok Stronghold's Alliance quests in one guide: Ranath Nightstride in
# Dalaran, Farholde Keep's chain through Riverglades that opens the rest, one
# run through the dungeon, then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed
# over, so the guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chain, every quest a lead-in of the dungeon's ones in the data: Ashe
# Amberhall's 94879 Scraps of Knowledge -> Demar Brant's 94886 The Western
# Front (to Sergeant Riftan) -> 94888 No Soldier Left Behind and 94889
# Carving a Path -> 94890 Bring Me His Head -> Riftan's 94983 Twilight
# Mementos (Twilight Bangles) and Demar Brant's 94982 Eye of Mugg. Ashe's 94881
# Curious Trinkets -> 94907 A Small Favor -> 94984 Tome of Twilight. Riftan's
# 94997 Lingering Essence follows 94983, to Ashe. Ranath Nightstride in
# Dalaran gives 96771 Vengeance of the Highborne (Zalfan Moonshadow, inside).
# Inside, Tunk's Krol'dok Moulding (item 267138) starts 94980 Krol'dok
# Moulding, for Alphonse Dumas, who gives 94981 Key Ingredients.
#
# Left out: nothing of the Alliance's.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Tunk or Zalfan Moonshadow
# inside, so their goals stand at the door (@37.5,38.2) with `group 5`. The
# bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon journal (Slavecrusher Grox,
# Twilight Commander Zarmok, Handler Ashka, Nar'gurk, Overseer Mugg), not of a
# recorded run. Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group that
# takes them in another order still gets each step ticked. Riverglades has
# only Forever's map frame, so typed coordinates are `coords live`.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The scouts' spot is the data's for that
#   objective.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - What drops where: the reference data: the bangles from the Twilight
#   Grunts and Warlocks and Zarmok, the tome from Nar'gurk, the eye from Mugg,
#   the moulding from Tunk (an elite inside).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   40 to 47).
# - Mob levels from data/forever set the waits: the Twilight on the western
#   front 42 to 44, the Twilight Thrall 44, Overlord Kilgar 46 (an elite).
# INGAME: where inside do Tunk and Zalfan Moonshadow stand?

